Web-parity notes (NOT silent drift)
  - The web `['notification-logs']` prefix invalidation is reproduced as refreshLogsFamily(): every
    OBSERVED feed whose key starts with "notification-logs:" (flat list, grouped, bell preview, AND
    unread-count) is re-fetched at once by each inbox write. unread-count is deliberately keyed under
    that prefix so the bell badge refreshes with the inbox, exactly like web.
  - groupMembers reuses the flat-list endpoint AND its cache key (filters + group_key merged), so an
    expand-row payload dedupes with a matching flat list (web `useGroupMembers` keys on logsFiltered).
  - The channel list read + channel write responses reuse the existing NotificationChannel union and
    `channelsKey()` ("channels") from the notificationchannels package — web shares the
    `['notification-channels']` cache between useNotificationChannels and useWebhookChannels.
  - Optimistic UI (instant inbox row flips) and toasts are render-layer concerns, intentionally not
    reproduced in the UI-free holder; the data-layer truth is the targeted refresh above.

